content.text:
The `p:nth-of-type(91)` white-on-white must be in the comparison section. The `grayBg` has `color: #f4f7fa` (same as background) — that's the bug! Let me check:

Looking at comparison.module.css line 21-27:
```css
.grayBg {
  color: #f4f7fa;
  background-color: #f4f7fa;
```

This sets both color AND background to `#f4f7fa`, making text invisible. But wait — the audit shows `ratio=1.00 fg=rgb(255, 255, 255) bg=rgb(255, 255, 255)`. The `#f4f7fa` is not white. Let me re-examine.

The `p:nth-of-type(91)` shows white on white. Looking at the resolution banner which has a white BG in the `descBlock` inside the `skycolorBg`. Actually, let me re-examine - the `descBlock` has `background-color: #fff` and `paragraphSmallText` has `color: #2b2b2b`. Not white-on-white.

The audit shows `fg=rgb(255, 255, 255) bg=rgb(255, 255, 255)`. This is white text on white background. The `grayBg` has `color: #f4f7fa` which is near-white but not pure white. Let me find the exact issue.

